  "captions": [
    {
      "scene": "01-bug",
      "text": "You maintain a Python library. This helper should remove duplicates without changing the caller's original list.",
      "startMs": 1163,
      "endMs": 11165
    },
    {
      "scene": "01-bug",
      "text": "The input contains elm twice. The current output keeps both copies. The required output keeps the first elm, then ash and birch.",
      "startMs": 11165,
      "endMs": 20166
    },
    {
      "scene": "01-bug",
      "text": "You ask for a fix. PatchProof checks the model's proposed code, then keeps the patch and results together for your review.",
      "startMs": 20166,
      "endMs": 29167
    },
    {
      "scene": "02-patch",
      "text": "The original condition only compares with the previous item. The proposed condition checks every item already kept.",
      "startMs": 29596,
      "endMs": 40597
    },
    {
      "scene": "02-patch",
      "text": "The model can edit solution.py. The check definitions stay outside that file; a separate runner tests the proposal.",
      "startMs": 40597,
      "endMs": 51598
    },
    {
      "scene": "03-decision",
      "text": "Before repair, 5 of 9 checks passed. This proposal passes all 9, including unchanged input and TypeError for None.",
      "startMs": 52047,
      "endMs": 63048
    },
    {
      "scene": "03-decision",
      "text": "A passing result covers the listed cases. You still inspect the full patch and decide whether to use it. Nothing is merged automatically.",
      "startMs": 63048,
      "endMs": 74050
    },
    {
      "scene": "04-failure",
      "text": "Here is a separate repair that failed. Rows become columns, but a real null cell must stay null. The fill value is only for missing cells.",
      "startMs": 74479,
      "endMs": 85480
    },
    {
      "scene": "04-failure",
      "text": "This patch still replaces null with 9. Only 11 of 13 checks pass, so it is not accepted. Later attempts had check errors.",
      "startMs": 85480,
      "endMs": 96480
    },
    {
      "scene": "05-evidence",
      "text": "The full patch stays available for human review. Download evidence saves the code change, requirements, observations and run details.",
      "startMs": 97134,
      "endMs": 105135
    },
    {
      "scene": "05-evidence",
      "text": "The standard repair also passed this example. These saved runs explain the workflow; they do not establish a benchmark advantage.",
      "startMs": 105135,
      "endMs": 113135
    },
    {
      "scene": "06-try-repair",
      "text": "To try it yourself, choose a curated Python task and select Generate patch. It starts a new model run and checks the proposal.",
      "startMs": 113641,
      "endMs": 120642
    },
    {
      "scene": "06-try-repair",
      "text": "Then review the patch and its results. This public demo uses curated examples; it does not accept your own repository.",
      "startMs": 120642,
      "endMs": 127643
    }
  ],
